# libdd is not compiled with sanitizers so probably that's why we get these
# data races from ddog_ArrayQueue and Datadog::Sample operations
race:ddog_ArrayQueue
race:Datadog::Sample::

# The fork handler cancels an in-flight upload from the forking thread. The cancellation
# wakes the exporter's tokio runtime by writing to its eventfd, and the upload thread then
# closes that eventfd when it drops the exporter. tokio orders the two with atomic reference
# counts inside libdatadog, which TSan cannot see. TSan only sees the ordering when the
# upload thread wakes up from epoll_wait after the write, so it reports a false race on the
# file descriptor when the upload thread notices the cancellation without waking up that way.
race:tokio::runtime::driver::Handle
